course: dictionary
lesson: 15087
title: Roadworthiness: is it safe to drive?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Roadworthiness is a noun. It tells you whether a vehicle is safe and fit to be driven on the road. «Dad took the van for its roadworthiness test on Monday.» The test checks whether the van is safe, so roadworthiness here means the van's state of being fit to drive.
explain: Look at the parts of the word: road, worthy, ness. Worthy means good enough for something, so roadworthy means good enough for the road. The ending -ness turns the adjective into a noun, just as kind becomes kindness. «The mechanic checked the brakes, lights and tyres before giving the car a certificate of roadworthiness.»
explain: Roadworthiness is uncountable, so you do not add an s or say a roadworthiness. You say «The car has good roadworthiness» or «The car has poor roadworthiness». Use the adjective roadworthy when you describe the vehicle itself: «The bus is roadworthy.»
fact: Roadworthiness means the state of a vehicle being safe and fit to be driven on the road.
fact: Roadworthiness is uncountable: say «good roadworthiness», not «a roadworthiness».
fact: A «roadworthiness test» is a check that a vehicle must pass to show it is safe to drive.
fact: Each country has its own name for this check: the MOT in the UK, the NCT in Ireland, and the WOF in New Zealand.
fact: In Australia, a «roadworthy certificate» shows that a vehicle has passed its safety check.
exercise: «Dad took the van for a roadworthiness test.» What does roadworthiness mean? | The speed a car can reach on a motorway | *The state of being safe and fit to be driven on the road | The colour a car is painted | A type of road sign
exercise: «The garage gave the car a certificate of roadworthiness.» What does this certificate show? | *That the car is safe and fit to drive on the road | That the car is the fastest in town | That the car is for sale
exercise: Which word is the adjective that goes with roadworthiness? | roadways | *roadworthy | worthless | roadside
test: «The car failed its check because its brakes were unsafe.» What does this show about the car's roadworthiness? | The car had a red door | *The car was not safe enough to drive | The car was brand new | The car was the best in the street
test: Which country calls its vehicle safety check the MOT? | Australia | *The United Kingdom | Ireland | New Zealand
exam: Which sentence uses roadworthiness correctly? | *The car has good roadworthiness, so it passed its check. | The car was roadworthiness and fast. | The car is roadworthiness on the road. | The car had roadworthinesses last week.
